<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Which match servers this build offers.

    A comma-separated list, each entry either an address or `Label=address` — see `serverEntries`.
    The first is the default until the player chooses otherwise, and their choice is stored.

    This used to be empty, and the emptiness was the shipped value: a build with no address queues
    nothing and submits nothing, which is a supported configuration rather than a broken one
    (`MatchReporter.None`). That was correct while there was no server to name. There is one now —
    tto.moebiuscore.fr, deployed from the `tto-server` repository — so a release build that offered
    no way to reach it would be offering the player less than exists.

    **HTTPS, and it has to be.** Accounts and passwords cross this connection, and Android's default
    network security policy refuses cleartext anyway. The certificate is a public Let's Encrypt one,
    so nothing here needs pinning or a network security configuration.

    A resource and not a constant, still, for the reason that has not changed: pointing a build at a
    staging host is a resource override rather than a code change. The debug variant overrides this
    with the local container — see `src/debug/res/values/server.xml`.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="servers" translatable="false">Moebius=https://tto.moebiuscore.fr</string>
</resources>
